/* ============================================================================
   FIELD-TEX.JS · the ground under tab 05                 (owner: condition.js)

   One JPEG, base64, as a data URI. It is here rather than beside the page as a
   .jpg for the same reason the meshes are: on file:// this app is not allowed
   to fetch() a local file, and a <script> tag is. A data: URI also goes
   straight into THREE.TextureLoader through an <img>, which needs no network
   at all — so the "Works offline" badge in the header stays honest.

   Injected lazily by condition.js the first time tab 05 is opened. A student
   who never reaches the drill never pays the 145 kB.

   Source: generated for this app (Higgsfield, nano_banana_pro), 1024 square,
   downscaled to 512 and JPEG-78. It is tiled 22x22 across a 120 m plane, so a
   tile is about 5.5 m of grass — detail past 512 is not reachable by any
   camera this drill uses.
   ========================================================================== */
window.FIELD_TEX = {
  grass: 'data:image/jpeg;base64,'
};
